# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 2: a bare `return` in the body ends the execution -- the plan stops
# there (REVIEW 0c601ea, the lesson of e8b8a8d), so `n: n + 5U` never runs: n is 1, not 6.  The root
# executes it from its nested bodies too -- an anonymous block (no inert one, l2_body_inert) and an
# if body.  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + 1U
    return
    n: n + 5U
return
size_t: a 9U
---
    Counter
a: Counter\n
Counter\n: 4U
if: a = 1U
    Counter
size_t: b 9U
b: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: a = 1U && b = 1U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
